tags: chat-stored

A limit of the node: the most messages of celaut-chat that the node keeps for one client.

The value is an integer in messages. Example: 200. Above the limit, the node deletes the oldest messages of the client.

The limit has no scope.

An absent limit is not a promise of no limit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=limit
name=chat-stored
per=one client
rule=Above the limit, the node deletes the oldest messages of the client.
scope=none
unit=messages
